WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:03.050
Ask a computer for zero point one plus zero

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.025
point two

3
00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:06.225
and it says zero point three

4
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.650
followed by a four

5
00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:09.300
far down the line

6
00:00:10.425 --> 00:00:11.450
Not a bug

7
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.900
A binary computer cannot write one tenth exactly

8
00:00:16.025 --> 00:00:18.875
the way decimal cannot write one third

9
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.375
It stores the nearest fraction it can

10
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:23.975
with fifty two bits

11
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.100
Add two of those

12
00:00:26.137 --> 00:00:27.625
and the rounding shows

13
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.275
So never compare floats with equals

14
00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:35.000
Compare the difference to a tiny epsilon

